    },
    "authorAssociation": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Hi! I've had these keymaps in my config for a while now and I only just thought to suggest them for inclusion in mini.basics.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gP\", '\"+P', { desc = \"Paste from system clipboard\" })\r\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gY\", '\"+y$', { desc = \"Copy rest of line to system clipboard\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nI remember when I first started using this plugin I tried `gY` on several occasions and always wondered why it wasn't working until I eventually figured out it just wasn't a thing haha. Obviously this was before I figured out how to read(!)\r\n\r\nWhen I added `gY` I figured `gP` just made sense as well.\r\n\r\nI think these are obvious extensions to the existing `gy` and `gp` keymaps which would fit great in mini.basics, what do you think?",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hi! I've had these keymaps in my config for a while now and I only just thought to suggest them for inclusion in mini.basics.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;gP&quot;, '&quot;+P', { desc = &quot;Paste from system clipboard&quot; })\nvim.keymap.set(&quot;n&quot;, &quot;gY&quot;, '&quot;+y$', { desc = &quot;Copy rest of line to system clipboard&quot; })\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>gP<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>\"+P<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Paste from system clipboard<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">keymap</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">set</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>n<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>gY<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>\"+y$<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span>, { <span class=\"pl-smi\">desc</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>Copy rest of line to system clipboard<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>})</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I remember when I first started using this plugin I tried <code class=\"notranslate\">gY</code> on several occasions and always wondered why it wasn't working until I eventually figured out it just wasn't a thing haha. Obviously this was before I figured out how to read(!)</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">When I added <code class=\"notranslate\">gY</code> I figured <code class=\"notranslate\">gP</code> just made sense as well.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think these are obvious extensions to the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">gy</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">gp</code> keymaps which would fit great in mini.basics, what do you think?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Hi! I've had these keymaps in my config for a while now and I only just thought to suggest them for inclusion in mini.basics.\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gP\", '\"+P', { desc = \"Paste from system clipboard\" })\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"gY\", '\"+y$', { desc = \"Copy rest of line to system clipboard\" })\nI remember when I first started using this plugin I tried gY on several occasions and always wondered why it wasn't working until I eventually figured out it just wasn't a thing haha. Obviously this was before I figured out how to read(!)\nWhen I added gY I figured gP just made sense as well.\nI think these are obvious extensions to the existing gy and gp keymaps which would fit great in mini.basics, what do you think?",
