            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Hello!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> I think these are obvious extensions to the existing `gy` and `gp` keymaps which would fit great in mini.basics, what do you think?\r\n\r\nI do not completely disagree, but having both `gp` and `gP` definitely feels a bit too much.\r\n\r\nThe `gY` is an interesting idea, though. My problems with it are that it is somewhat narrow and would imply that `gP` should be added (which I don't think is needed). I'll need time to think about it a bit more.",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello!</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I think these are obvious extensions to the existing <code class=\"notranslate\">gy</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">gp</code> keymaps which would fit great in mini.basics, what do you think?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I do not completely disagree, but having both <code class=\"notranslate\">gp</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">gP</code> definitely feels a bit too much.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">gY</code> is an interesting idea, though. My problems with it are that it is somewhat narrow and would imply that <code class=\"notranslate\">gP</code> should be added (which I don't think is needed). I'll need time to think about it a bit more.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Hello!\n\nI think these are obvious extensions to the existing gy and gp keymaps which would fit great in mini.basics, what do you think?\n\nI do not completely disagree, but having both gp and gP definitely feels a bit too much.\nThe gY is an interesting idea, though. My problems with it are that it is somewhat narrow and would imply that gP should be added (which I don't think is needed). I'll need time to think about it a bit more.",
